1
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:17,430
Rach, we're running low on resumes over here.

2
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,430
Do you really want a job with Popular Mechanics?

3
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,890
Well, if you're gonna work for mechanics, those are the ones to work for.

4
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,480
Hey, look, you guys. I'm going for anything here, okay?

5
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,690
I can't be a waitress anymore. I mean it.

6
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,570
I'm sick of the lousy tips. I'm sick of being called "Excuse Me."

7
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:37,570
Rach, did you proofread these?

8
00:00:37,780 --> 00:00:39,580
Uh, yeah. Why?

9
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:45,410
Uh, nothing. I'm sure they'll be impressed with your excellent "compuper" skills.

10
00:00:45,580 --> 00:00:48,000
Oh, my God!

11
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:50,710
Oh, do you think it's on all of them?

12
00:00:53,970 --> 00:00:57,340
Oh, no, I'm sure the Xerox machine caught a few.

13
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:50,650
Hey, guys. 

14
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:53,270
Hey. Hi, ladies.

15
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:55,940
Uh, can I get you anything?

16
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:58,030
Did you bring the mail?

17
00:01:56,110 --> 00:01:58,030
 Lots of responses.

18
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:01,120
Really? Sure we have scones left.

19
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:03,080
Okay, read them to me.

20
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:07,830
Dear Miss Green: Thank you for your inquiry. However...

21
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,080
We have apple cinnamon...  

22
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:11,080
Okay, "Dear Miss Green"...

23
00:02:11,250 --> 00:02:14,420
Yeah. Yeah, yeah. No.

24
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:17,630
What?

25
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,220
Your Visa bill is huge.

26
00:02:21,090 --> 00:02:22,140
Give me that.

27
00:02:22,510 --> 00:02:24,430
You know, I can't believe you. Linda is so great.

28
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,640
Why won't you go out with her again? 

29
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:26,640
I don't know.

30
00:02:26,810 --> 00:02:28,560
Is this still about her whole...

31
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:31,230
..."The Flintstones could have really happened" thing?

32
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:33,690
It's not just that.

33
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:36,690
It's just, I want someone who does something for me...

34
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:38,780
...you know, who gets my heart pounding...

35
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,860
...who makes me, uh...

36
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:46,030
Little play things with yarn?

37
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:49,000
What?

38
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,710
Could you want her more?

39
00:02:52,330 --> 00:02:53,330
Who?

40
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,050
Who? Dee, the sarcastic sister from What's Happening!!

41
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,180
Look, I am totally, totally over her, okay?

42
00:03:07,350 --> 00:03:08,930
I just... Hi.

43
00:03:07,350 --> 00:03:08,930
Hi. Coffee?

44
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:11,480
No, we're fine. 

45
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:11,480
Okay.

46
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,900
Shut up.

47
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:19,940
We're not saying anything.

48
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:23,200
What?

49
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:23,200
Uh,Joey cried last night.

50
00:03:24,030 --> 00:03:25,660
Thank you.

51
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,410
We were playing poker, right?

52
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:30,540
There was chocolate on the three. It looked like an eight, all right?

53
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:35,540
Oh, God, you should've seen him. "Read them and weep."

54
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:37,630
And then he did.

55
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:42,550
Well, now, how come you guys have never played poker with us?

56
00:03:42,720 --> 00:03:44,840
Yeah, what is that? Like some kind of guy thing?

57
00:03:45,010 --> 00:03:46,890
Like some kind of sexist guy thing?

58
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:49,390
Like, it's poker, so only guys can play?

59
00:03:49,770 --> 00:03:51,230
No. Women are welcome to play.

60
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:52,730
Oh, okay, so then what is it?

61
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:56,190
Some kind of, you know, like, some kind of, you know, like...

62
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:58,190
All right, what is it?

63
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:02,030
There just don't happen to be any women in our game.

64
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:06,070
Yeah, we just don't happen to know any women that know how to play poker.

65
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:10,240
Oh, please. That is such a lame excuse. I mean, it's a typical guy response.

66
00:04:10,410 --> 00:04:12,370
Excuse me, do any of you know how to play?

67
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:14,040
No.

68
00:04:15,420 --> 00:04:16,750
But you could teach us.

69
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,420
No.

70
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:27,550
Okay, so now we draw cards.

71
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:33,020
So I wouldn't need any, right? Because I have a straight.

72
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,480
Oh, good for you.

73
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:35,480
Congratulations.

74
00:04:38,610 --> 00:04:40,440
Okay, Pheebs, how many do you want?

75
00:04:40,690 --> 00:04:45,700
Okay, I just need two. The 10 of spades and the six of clubs.

76
00:04:47,450 --> 00:04:49,070
No, uh, Pheebs, you can't do that.

77
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:51,120
I have the 10 of spades. Here, you want it?

78
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:52,660
Thanks.

79
00:04:53,830 --> 00:04:56,370
Uh, no, see, uh, you can't do that.

80
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,920
No, no. That's okay. I don't need them. I'm going for fours.

81
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:00,460
Oh, you're...

82
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:07,260
All right, here we go.

83
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:10,680
We've got salmon roulettes and assorted crudits.

84
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:12,640
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Monica, what are you doing?

85
00:05:12,810 --> 00:05:16,640
This is a poker game. You can't serve food with more than one syllable.

86
00:05:16,810 --> 00:05:20,270
It's got to be like chips or dip or pretz...

87
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,320
Okay, so at this point, the dealer...

88
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:28,160
You know what? We got it. We got it. Let's play for real. High stakes. Big bucks.

89
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:30,700
All right, now, you sure? Phoebe just threw away two jacks...

90
00:05:30,870 --> 00:05:32,580
...because they didn't look happy.

91
00:05:36,790 --> 00:05:39,960
But I'm ready. So just deal.

92
00:05:40,130 --> 00:05:43,090
Okay, all right, last minute lesson. Last minute lesson. Joey.

93
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:44,760
Three...

94
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,420
...eight.

95
00:05:46,590 --> 00:05:48,590
Eight, three. All right. Here we go.

96
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,770
Damn it, damn it, damn it.

97
00:05:55,930 --> 00:05:58,560
I see. So then, um, you were lying.

98
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:01,020
About what?

99
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:01,020
About how good your cards were.

100
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:02,940
Heh. I was bluffing.

101
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:06,190
Aha. And what is "bluffing"?

102
00:06:07,950 --> 00:06:11,160
Is it not another word for lying?

103
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,660
Okay, sorry to break up this party...

104
00:06:13,830 --> 00:06:16,040
...but I've got resumes to fax before work tomorrow.

105
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,500
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

106
00:06:16,200 --> 00:06:18,500
Rach, we've got to settle.

107
00:06:18,660 --> 00:06:20,420
Settle what?

108
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:23,590
The Jamestown colony of Virginia.

109
00:06:25,460 --> 00:06:28,550
You see, King George is giving us the land, so...

110
00:06:31,300 --> 00:06:34,470
The game, Rachel. The game. You owe us money for the game.

111
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:35,720
Oh, right.

112
00:06:35,890 --> 00:06:39,350
You know what, guys? It's their first time. Why don't we forget about the money?

113
00:06:39,520 --> 00:06:42,150
Hell, no. We'll pay.

114
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:45,570
Okay, Monica, I had another answer all ready.

115
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:48,190
And you know what?

116
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,030
We want a rematch. 

117
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:51,030
Well, that's fine with me.

118
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,240
Could use the money.

119
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:58,450
So, basically, you get your ya-yas by taking money from all of your friends.

120
00:06:59,370 --> 00:07:02,790
Yes,and I get my ya-yas from lkea.

121
00:07:04,880 --> 00:07:08,510
You have to put them together yourself, but they cost a little less.

122
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:12,590
Look, Rachel, this is poker. I play to win, all right?

123
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,100
In order for me to win, other people have to lose.

124
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:18,850
So if you're gonna play poker with me, don't expect me to be a nice guy.

125
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:22,020
Okay, because once those cards are dealt...

126
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,610
Yeah?

127
00:07:35,950 --> 00:07:38,080
I'm not a nice guy.

128
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:46,500
All right, boys. Let's eat.

129
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:50,300
Ah, did you get that from the "I Love Rachel" pizzeria?

130
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,510
You still on that? 

131
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,510
Come on.

132
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,840
What was with that whole Black Bart speech?

133
00:07:55,010 --> 00:07:58,430
When I play poker, I'm not a nice guy.

134
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:00,600
You're way off, pal.

135
00:08:00,770 --> 00:08:04,940
No, I don't think so. See, Ross, because I think you love her.

136
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:06,310
Uh, no.

137
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:09,820
See, I might have had feelings for her at one time. Not anymore.

138
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:12,690
I just... Marcel.

139
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:16,240
Where are you going with that disk? You are not putting that on again.

140
00:08:16,410 --> 00:08:21,940
Marcel... Okay. If you press that button, you are in very, very big trouble.

141
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:38,430
You believe what a jerk Ross was being?

142
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,010
Yeah, I know. He can get really competitive.

143
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,810
What?

144
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:49,690
Oh. "Hello, Kettle, this is Monica. You're black."

145
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:51,650
Please.

146
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:56,660
I am not as bad as Ross.

147
00:08:56,820 --> 00:09:00,280
Oh, I beg to differ. The Pictionary incident?

148
00:09:00,990 --> 00:09:02,490
That was not an incident.

149
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:07,250
I was gesturing and the plate slipped out of my hand.

150
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:14,630
Oh! I got an interview. I got an interview.

151
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:14,630
You're kidding. Where? Where?

152
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:19,390
Saks Fifth Avenue.

153
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:19,390
Oh, Rachel.

154
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:23,060
Oh, it's like the mother ship is calling you home.

155
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,110
Well, what's the job?

156
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:30,110
Assistant buyer.

157
00:09:30,270 --> 00:09:33,820
Oh! I would be shopping...

158
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:36,900
...for a living.

159
00:09:38,950 --> 00:09:40,320
Okay, look. That's Aunt Iris.

160
00:09:40,490 --> 00:09:42,830
This woman has been playing poker since she was 5.

161
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:45,330
You've gotta listen to every word she says.

162
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,710
Is Tony Randall dead?

163
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,290
Oh, why?   

164
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,290
I don't think so.

165
00:09:49,460 --> 00:09:52,500
Well, he may be now because I think I hit him with my car.

166
00:09:52,710 --> 00:09:56,260
My God. Really? 

167
00:09:52,710 --> 00:09:56,260
No, that's bluffing. Lesson number one.

168
00:09:58,260 --> 00:09:59,630
Let me tell you something.

169
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:03,390
Everything you hear at a poker game is pure crap.

170
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:05,930
Nice earrings.

171
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:05,930
Thank you.

172
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:10,560
Girls, sit down.

173
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:13,570
Um, Aunt Iris, this is Phoebe, and Rachel...

174
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:13,570
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

175
00:10:13,730 --> 00:10:16,780
Listen, I am parked at a meter. Let's do it.

176
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:29,580
Ross, could we please, please, listen to anything else?

177
00:10:29,750 --> 00:10:31,210
All right.

178
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,770
I'm gonna pay for that tonight.

179
00:10:54,940 --> 00:10:56,020
Hey.

180
00:10:56,190 --> 00:10:57,650
Guess what, guess what, guess what.

181
00:10:57,820 --> 00:11:02,740
Uh, okay. The fifth dentist caved, and now they're all recommending Trident?

182
00:11:08,750 --> 00:11:11,120
No, the interview.

183
00:11:11,290 --> 00:11:13,210
She loved me. She absolutely loved me.

184
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:17,090
We talked for, like, two and a half hours. We have the same taste in clothes.

185
00:11:17,380 --> 00:11:19,340
Oh, I went to camp with her cousin.

186
00:11:19,510 --> 00:11:23,050
And, oh, the job is perfect. I can do this. I can do this well.

187
00:11:23,220 --> 00:11:24,590
That's great.

188
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,550
God. And she told the funniest story.

189
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:28,680
Okay, great, you'll tell us and we'll laugh.

190
00:11:28,850 --> 00:11:30,770
Let's play poker.

191
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:34,230
All right, listen, we talked about it...

192
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,940
...and if you don't want to play, we completely understand.

193
00:11:37,110 --> 00:11:40,190
Yes, yes. We can play some other game. Like, I don't know...

194
00:11:40,360 --> 00:11:41,990
...Pictionary?

195
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:45,160
Very funny. Very funny.

196
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,780
I think we'd like to give poker another try. Shall we, ladies?

197
00:11:47,950 --> 00:11:49,450
Yes, I think we should.

198
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:51,200
Rach, do you want me to shuffle those?

199
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:54,000
No, no. That's okay. You know what? I'm gonna give it a go.

200
00:11:54,170 --> 00:11:55,380
All right.

201
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:09,560
So Pheebs owes 7.50. Monica, you owe $10.

202
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:12,730
And, Rachel, you owe 15 big ones.

203
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:15,690
Thanks for teaching us "Crossed-eyed Mary."

204
00:12:15,860 --> 00:12:18,190
You guys, we gotta play that other way.

205
00:12:19,730 --> 00:12:23,650
All right, here's my 7.50, but I think you should know that this money is cursed.

206
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:26,280
What?

207
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:26,280
Oh,I cursed it.

208
00:12:27,990 --> 00:12:30,700
So now bad things will happen to he who spends it.

209
00:12:31,450 --> 00:12:34,580
That's all right, I'll take it. Bad things happen to me anyway.

210
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:38,210
This way, I can break them up with a movie.

211
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:43,760
So that just leaves the big Green poker machine, who owes 15.

212
00:12:43,970 --> 00:12:46,130
Hmm, oh, it's so typical:

213
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:48,760
Ooh, I'm a man. Ooh, I have a penis.

214
00:12:48,930 --> 00:12:52,810
Ooh, I have to win money to exert my power over women.

215
00:12:56,350 --> 00:12:57,850
You know what? This is not over.

216
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:01,270
We will play you again. And we will win and you will lose.

217
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:03,190
And you will beg and we will laugh.

218
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,200
And we will take every last dime you have.

219
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:08,240
And you will hate yourselves forever.

220
00:13:09,830 --> 00:13:13,330
Hmm. Kind of stepped on my point there, Mon.

221
00:13:19,460 --> 00:13:21,540
So you gals wanna hand over your money now?

222
00:13:21,710 --> 00:13:24,840
That way, we don't have to go through the formality of actually playing.

223
00:13:25,720 --> 00:13:30,570
No, that's fine. We'll see who has the last laugh there, monkey boy.

224
00:13:32,890 --> 00:13:36,020
Okay, are we done with the chitchat? Are we ready to play serious poker?

225
00:13:36,230 --> 00:13:39,940
Hey, you guys, look. The one-eyed jack follows me wherever I go.

226
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:43,480
Right, okay. Serious poker.

227
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:46,900
Excuse me. Where are you going?

228
00:13:47,070 --> 00:13:48,400
Uh, to the bathroom.

229
00:13:48,570 --> 00:13:50,950
Do you wanna go to the bathroom or do you wanna play poker?

230
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:52,780
I wanna go to the bathroom.

231
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,790
All right, well, I'm gonna order a pizza. 

232
00:13:55,120 --> 00:13:57,790
Oh, no, no, no.

233
00:13:57,960 --> 00:13:59,370
I'm waiting to hear from that job.

234
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:02,130
And the store closes at 9, so you can eat then.

235
00:14:02,960 --> 00:14:06,970
That's fine. I'll just have a Tic Tac to hold me over.

236
00:14:07,930 --> 00:14:12,300
All right. Cincinnati. No blinds. Everybody ante.

237
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,310
Yes.

238
00:14:14,850 --> 00:14:16,520
Or no.

239
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:19,940
All right.

240
00:14:20,100 --> 00:14:21,730
Your money's mine, Green.

241
00:14:21,900 --> 00:14:23,610
Your fly's open, Geller.

242
00:14:29,610 --> 00:14:31,280
You guys, you know what I just realized?

243
00:14:32,370 --> 00:14:35,450
Joker is "poker" with a "J."

244
00:14:37,830 --> 00:14:39,410
Coincidence?

245
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:44,590
Hey, that's "jo-incidence" with a "C."

246
00:14:55,010 --> 00:14:58,600
Uh, Phoebe. Phoebe... 

247
00:14:55,010 --> 00:14:58,600
Yeah, I'm out.

248
00:14:59,350 --> 00:15:00,640
I'm in.

249
00:15:00,810 --> 00:15:02,020
Me too.

250
00:15:02,190 --> 00:15:03,980
Me too. All right. What do you got?

251
00:15:04,900 --> 00:15:09,400
Well, you better hop out of the shower, because I got a flush.

252
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:14,070
Well, well, well.

253
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:18,910
Hop back in, bucko, because I got four sixes.

254
00:15:19,080 --> 00:15:22,120
I got four sixes. I won. I actually won.

255
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:26,540
Oh, my God. You know what? I think I'm gonna make a little Ross pile.

